        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ce8bf2b7-c610-5dba-9087-3eea7e815a33",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Fowle Baldwin, George Rumford Baldwin, Loammi Baldwin, Loammi Baldwin Jr., Cyrus Baldwin, Benjamin Franklin Baldwin\n- Projects: Middlesex Canal, Boston and Lowell Railroad, Boston and Albany Railroad, Boston, Hartford, and Erie Railroad, Buffalo and Mississippi Railroad, Lake Cochituate water supply, Quebec gas and water systems\n- Companies: Boston and Maine Railroad\n- Places: Massachusetts, Boston, Quebec\n\nFacts:\n- James Fowle Baldwin was born on April 29, 1782, and died on May 20, 1862.\n- George Rumford Baldwin was born in North Woburn on January 26, 1798, and died there on October 11, 1888.\n- James Fowle Baldwin was an early American civil engineer who worked with his father and brothers on the Middlesex Canal and many other early engineering projects.\n- George Rumford Baldwin was an early American civil engineer who worked with his father Loammi Baldwin and his brothers Loammi Baldwin Jr., Cyrus Baldwin, Benjamin Franklin Baldwin, and James Fowle Baldwin on the Middlesex Canal and other projects.\n- James Fowle Baldwin surveyed and designed the Boston and Lowell Railroad, the Boston and Albany Railroad, and Boston's first water supply from Lake Cochituate.\n- The Boston and Lowell Railroad was a historic railroad that operated in Massachusetts in the United States.\n- The Boston and Lowell Railroad later operated as part of the Boston and Maine Railroad's Southern Division.\n- George Rumford Baldwin later surveyed and engineered the Boston, Hartford, and Erie Railroad, the Buffalo and Mississippi Railroad, and the gas and water systems for the City of Quebec.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9801f13a-1df0-5fa7-91fd-13ead6edf71b",
        "text": "Page: James Fowle Baldwin. Sentence: James Fowle Baldwin (April 29, 1782 – May 20, 1862) was an early American civil engineer who worked with his father and brothers on the Middlesex Canal, surveyed and designed the Boston and Lowell Railroad and the Boston and Albany Railroad, the first Boston water supply from Lake Cochituate, and many other early engineering projects.\nPage: Boston and Lowell Railroad. Sentence: The Boston and Lowell Railroad is a historic railroad that operated in Massachusetts in the United States.\nPage: Boston and Lowell Railroad. Sentence: The line later operated as part of the Boston and Maine Railroad's Southern Division.\nPage: George Rumford Baldwin. Sentence: George Rumford Baldwin (North Woburn, January 26, 1798 – North Woburn, October 11, 1888) an early American civil engineer who worked with his father Loammi Baldwin and brothers Loammi Baldwin, Jr. Cyrus Baldwin, Benjamin Franklin Baldwin, and James Fowle Baldwin, on the Middlesex Canal and other projects.\nPage: George Rumford Baldwin. Sentence: His later works included surveying and engineering the Boston, Hartford, and Erie Railroad, the Buffalo and Mississippi Railroad, and the gas and water systems for the City of Quebec.",
